      "summary": "Add `@tangleai/os`, a browser operating system for applications built on Jaren and Tangle. A module is a JSON manifest plus the contract operations it serves and needs; the desktop hosts it as a shipped component, as a jaren-app document in a sandboxed opaque-origin frame, or as an application's own page on its own origin that joins with `connectToOs` from `@tangleai/os/module`. The kernel installs modules in shipped, suite and user layers with RFC 6902 patches, keeps a journal with undo and a recovery boot, routes every call between modules as a contract operation under grants into a ledger, carries mail, and lists every granted operation as an assistant tool. The assistant's model placeholder and the documentation now name only the models that write Jaren's JSON documents reliably: `anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5`, and Qwen 3.7 27B or larger. The desktop has context menus on its background, title bars and dock, minimized windows now actually hide, and `mountDesktop` takes `themeFor` and `onSchemeSwitch` so a host's own colours survive the dock's light/dark switch. The Pages desktop ships an Assistant window and a Settings app: provider, OpenRouter key (kept in this browser, optionally for the tab only), region, a model picker over OpenRouter's catalogue, appearance, and forgetting what the browser keeps.",
      "id": "os-browser-desktop"
    }
